    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d411-a2">

                <pb facs="1206" n="1056" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg1056"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Consul-General Ravndal to Ambassador
                    Leishman.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Beirut</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-05-13"><hi rendition="#italic">May 13,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Customs director here has received a telegram from Constantinople that all
                    American establishments in Syria have been officially recognized and that they
                    must be accorded immunities. Americans here rejoicing, including myself. Send
                    you hearty felicitations and thanks.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ravndal.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
